    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Describe the numbers that have exactly five factors.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Fourth powers of prime numbers: $p^4$, where $p$ is prime.",
          "worked": "The five factors of $p^4$, where $p$ is prime, are $1,p,p^2,p^3,p^4$.\n\nConversely, a number with five factors has two factor pairs and a repeated middle factor, so it is a square. If it had two different prime factors $p$ and $q$, its square structure would give at least the six distinct factors $1,p,q,pq,p^2,q^2$. Hence it has only one prime factor and is a power $p^k$. Its factors are $1,p,\\ldots,p^k$, so $k+1=5$ and $k=4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the smallest four-digit number with exactly five factors.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$7^4=2401$.",
          "worked": "By part (a), the number must be the fourth power of a prime. The primes up to $7$ give\n$$2^4=16,\\quad 3^4=81,\\quad 5^4=625,\\quad 7^4=2401.$$\nFourth powers increase as the positive base increases. Therefore, the smallest four-digit number with exactly five factors is $2401$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the largest four-digit number with exactly five factors.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2401$.\n\nIt is the only four-digit fourth power of a prime.",
          "worked": "By part (a), the number must be $p^4$ for a prime $p$.\n$$7^4=2401,\\qquad 11^4=14641.$$\nThe primes $7$ and $11$ are consecutive, and $5^4=625$ has only three digits. Therefore, $2401$ is the only four-digit number with exactly five factors, so it is also the largest.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
